      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: AR-012 | Topic: Compound Interest | Subtopic: Multi-Year Geometric Growth | Difficulty: Moderate | Calculation: Low | Time: 35s | Originality Check: Verified Fresh | Correct Option: B\n• English Explanation:\n• Step 1 — Formula: In compound interest with annual compounding, amounts grow in geometric progression over equal intervals of time:\n(A_(4))/(A_(2))=(A_(2))/(P)\n• Step 2 — Substitution:\n(27,000)/(18,000)=(18,000)/(P)\n• Step 3 — Calculation:\n(3)/(2)=(18,000)/(P)⟹P=(18,000×2)/(3)=₹12,000 (Option B)\n• English Shortcut: P=((A_(2))^(2))/(A_(4))=(18,000×18,000)/(27,000)=₹12,000.\n• English Exam Tip: If a sum becomes X in T years and Y in 2T years at compound interest, Principal P=(X^(2))/(Y).",
