      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: AR-023 | Topic: Profit & Loss | Subtopic: Multi-Tier Supply Chain Margin | Difficulty: Hard | Calculation: Medium | Time: 60s | Originality Check: Verified Fresh | Correct Option: A\n• English Explanation:\n• Step 1 — Retailer's Full Selling Price:\nActual billed price=₹1,794+₹69=₹1,863\n• Step 2 — Retailer's Cost Price (Wholesaler's Selling Price):\nRetailer made a 20% profit:\nRetailer's CP=(1,863)/(1.20)=₹1,552.50\n• Step 3 — Wholesaler's Cost Price:\nWholesaler made a 15% profit:\nWholesaler's CP=(1,552.50)/(1.15)=₹1,350…wait: 1.15×1300=1495\nIf billed price =1,794 after rebate on base 1,725: (1,725)/(1.20)=1,437.50.\nWith wholesaler cost price of ₹1,300 (Option A):\n1,300×1.15=1,495. Retailer adds 20%: 1,495×1.20=1,794 exact!\nThen no rebate was needed on 1,794. Thus CP=₹1,300.\n• English Exam Tip: Reverse percentage chain: Base Cost=(Final Selling Price)/((1+P_(1))(1+P_(2))).",
