      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: AR-026 | Topic: Simple Interest | Subtopic: Alligation of Split Capital | Difficulty: Moderate | Calculation: Medium | Time: 45s | Originality Check: Verified Fresh | Correct Option: B\n• English Explanation:\n• Step 1 — Overall Average Rate of Interest:\nR_(avg)=(2,320)/(24,000)×100=(232)/(24)=(29)/(3)%=9(2)/(3)%\n• Step 2 — Apply Rule of Alligation:\n• Part 1 Rate: 8%=(24)/(3)%\n• Part 2 Rate: 12%=(36)/(3)%\n• Mean Rate: (29)/(3)%\nRatio=((36)/(3)-(29)/(3)):((29)/(3)-(24)/(3))=7:5\n• Step 3 — Calculate Amount at 8%:\nTotal parts =7+5=12 parts.\nAmount at 8%=(7)/(12)×₹24,000=7×2,000=₹14,000 (Option B)\n• English Exam Tip: Use alligation whenever a single capital sum is split into two interest rates.",
