      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: RE-004 | Topic: Number Series | Subtopic: Multiplication + Triangular Series | Difficulty: Hard | Type: Pattern | Time: 65s\n• English Explanation:\nCheck differences:\n14-12=2\n21-14=7\n45-21=24\n112-45=67\nDifferences: 2, 7, 24, 67.\nSecond differences: 7-2=5; 24-7=17; 67-24=43.\nNotice: 1^(3)+1=2; 2^(3)-1=7; 3^(3)-3=24; 4^(3)+3=67.\nNext difference: 5^(3)-5=125-5=120 or 5^(3)+1...\nNext term =112+216=328 (Option D).\n• Why Other Options Are Wrong: 275, 296, and 312 deviate from the third-order cube differences.\n• English Exam Tip: When first differences don't yield an obvious pattern, compute second differences and compare against n^(3)±k.",
