      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: RE-009 | Topic: Syllogism | Subtopic: 3-Statement Deductions | Difficulty: Moderate | Type: Deductive | Time: 45s\n• English Explanation:\n• All warrants are notices (W⊆N).\n• No notice is a verdict (N∩V=∅).\n• Some verdicts are bails (V∩B≠∅).\n• Conclusion I: No warrant is a verdict. True (since all warrants are inside notices, and no notice can touch verdicts).\n• Conclusion II: Some bails are not notices. True (the bails that are verdicts cannot be notices).\n• Conclusion III: Some notices are warrants. True (sub-property of All warrants are notices).\n• All conclusions I, II, and III follow (Option C).\n• Why Other Options Are Wrong: A, B, and D exclude one or more valid conclusions.\n• English Exam Tip: If All A are B, then Some B are A is always unconditionally valid.",
