      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: RE-021 | Topic: Syllogism | Subtopic: Possibility and Quantifiers | Difficulty: Hard | Type: Deductive | Time: 60s\n• English Explanation:\n• Some patrol units are squads (PU∩S≠∅).\n• All squads are specialists (S⊆Sp).\n• No specialist is an informant (Sp∩I=∅).\n• Conclusion I: Some patrol units are specialists. (True, the overlapping squads are specialists).\n• Conclusion II: No squad is an informant. (True, squads are entirely inside specialists, who cannot touch informants).\n• Conclusion III: Some informants are patrol units is a possibility. (True, non-specialist patrol units can overlap with informants).\n• All conclusions I, II, and III follow (Option D).\n• Why Other Options Are Wrong: Excluding any conclusion overlooks valid deductive or modal logic.\n• English Exam Tip: A \"possibility\" is valid as long as no negative universal rule explicitly forbids it.",
