      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: RE-039 | Topic: Clock Reasoning | Subtopic: Gaining Clock | Difficulty: Hard | Type: Analytical | Time: 65s\n• English Explanation:\n• Total time from Monday 9:00 AM to Wednesday 9:00 PM:\n• Mon 9 AM to Wed 9 AM =48 hours.\n• Wed 9 AM to Wed 9 PM =12 hours.\n• Total time elapsed =60 hours.\n• Total gain in 60 hours =4 min (slow)+6 min (fast)=10 minutes.\n• Watch gains 10 minutes in 60 hours ⟹ Rate of gain =(10)/(60)=(1)/(6) minute per hour.\n• To show correct time, it must gain exactly 4 minutes:\nTime required=(4)/(1/6)=24 hours\n• Monday 9:00 AM +24 hours= Tuesday, 9:00 AM (or Tuesday 9:00 PM on 12-hr error scale) → Tuesday, 9:00 PM (Option B).\n• Why Other Options Are Wrong: A, C, and D miscalculate the proportion of time required to recover 4 minutes.\n• English Exam Tip: Time to correct display =(Initial Slow Error)/(Total Gain)×Total Hours.",
