      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: GS2-013 | Topic: Indian Polity | Subtopic: Union Executive & Ordinances | Difficulty: Moderate | Concept: Article 123 Lapse Rules | Estimated Time: 35s | Duplicate Check: Passed\n• English Explanation: Under Article 123(2)(a), an Ordinance promulgated by the President must be laid before both Houses of Parliament and ceases to operate at the expiration of six weeks from the reassembly of Parliament, unless disapproved earlier.\n• Why Other Options Are Wrong:\n• A) Four weeks is insufficient under Article 123.\n• C) Eight weeks applies to some executive rules, not constitutional ordinances.\n• D) Six months is the maximum permissible gap between parliamentary sessions, not the lifespan post-reassembly.\n• English Exam Tip: Maximum life of an Ordinance without approval = 6 months (inter-session gap) + 6 weeks = ~7.5 months.",
