      "en": "• Question Metadata: ID: GS2-022 | Topic: Indian National Movement | Subtopic: Overseas Revolutionary Organizations | Difficulty: Moderate | Concept: Rash Behari Bose & Indian Independence League | Estimated Time: 35s | Duplicate Check: Passed\n• English Explanation: Veteran revolutionary Rash Behari Bose fled to Japan in 1915 and established the Indian Independence League at the Tokyo Conference in March 1942. He later handed over the leadership of the League and the INA to Subhas Chandra Bose in July 1943 at Singapore.\n• Why Other Options Are Wrong:\n• A) Subhas Chandra Bose assumed leadership of the League in 1943, creating the Provisional Government of Azad Hind.\n• C) Mohan Singh raised the initial First INA from British Indian POWs in Malaya.\n• D) Captain Lakshmi Sahgal headed the Rani of Jhansi Women's Regiment.\n• English Exam Tip: Founder of Indian Independence League (Japan, 1942) = Rash Behari Bose; Supreme Commander of Azad Hind Fauj = Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose.",
