      "en": "• Correct Answer: B (Suryapet)\n• English Explanation: Phanigiri is an internationally recognized Buddhist archaeological heritage site situated on a hilltop in Nagaram mandal of Suryapet district, Telangana. Excavations by the State Archaeology Department yielded magnificent Satavahana and Ikshvaku-era stupas, viharas, apsidal chaityagrihas, Roman gold coins, and an octagonal limestone pillar depicting Asokan motifs.\n• Why Other Options Are Wrong (English):\n• A) Nalgonda is noted for the Devarkonda and Rachakonda medieval hill forts.\n• C) Mahabubnagar is famous for Manyamkonda Venkateswara temple and Pillalamarri banyan tree.\n• D) Yadadri Bhuvanagiri is celebrated for the Yadagirigutta Lakshmi Narasimha temple and Kolanupaka Jain shrine.\n• English Exam Tip: Major Buddhist Sites in Telangana: Phanigiri (Suryapet), Nelakondapalli (Khammam), Dhulikatta (Peddapalli), Kotilingala (Jagtial).",
